{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1333115-wtf-2e-actual-play-spare-me-over","id":1333115,"title":"[WtF 2E Actual Play] Spare Me Over","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-29T10:10:26-07:00","id":1333115,"title":"[WtF 2E Actual Play] Spare Me Over","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#141414\">Hello Internet! I\u2019ve been spending the last month or so running a Wild West-inspired Werewolf the Forsaken 2E game over on discord, and I\u2019ve enjoyed it enough - so why not showcase this brilliant gameline with another AP?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\">My group consists of three longtime friends: Viskarenvisla, GriffinGuy21, and my crazy RL Partner: ZeiGal. We\u2019re all old hats to Werewolf, and we wanted to try a game where the characters were a little more established, and explore the creep factor within Werewolf itself. As Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon just released - it was the perfect storm for a new game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\">A few tidbits:</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">I have liberated ideas from nearly everywhere that\u2019s got Forsaken content. Predators, both Night Horrors, and the settings from Hunting Grounds: the Rockies and the Quickstart adventure are all bookmarked and referenced with mad glee. NateD\u2019s AP \u201cHome is Where the Bones Are\u201d is also a strong inspiration, as well as Visk\u2019s own APs with Mr. Shopping on RPG.net</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">We run this text-based, so the pacing might feel a bit off at some points. That\u2019s what happens when you\u2019ve got three players who like to have detailed conversations w/ NPCs. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">As is RPG.net tradition, OOC will be in BLUE as homage to BrokenDiamond.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Our starting year is 1863, and though I\u2019m trying to keep as true to the technology and culture of that time; the Rule of Cool is always gonna be picked over the Rule of Historical Accuracy.</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><span style=\"color:#141414\">Before I begin, allow me to pepper in the Hook and the characters that make up our vengeance-bound Pack</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\">The Hook:</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>The most dangerous lesson for the Uratha is that they might call the bulk of humanity the Herd, but that humans are not sheep.<br /> <br /> To hear the Urdaga speak of the inciting incident, it was the malicious nature of a pack of Predator Kings, but the actual issue has been lost to rumor, time, and death. What is known is that Someone, Somewhere Severely Wronged their Wolf-Blooded Kin. Blooded Kin that knew far too well the weaknesses and strengths of their Uratha cousins and had only one solution for the rabid beasts in their midst: Execution.<br /> <br /> Since that time, those Wolf-Blooded has become more than a simple family. They've become a Compact that roams far and wide throughout the open frontier of young America following the rumors of Werewolves and are serve as the boogeyman of many a Forsaken pack - native, or otherwise. <br /> <br /> Up until recently, you went along with them. Cursed with the Wolf's Blood, you were a willing participant in the slaughter of Beasts Damned by God.<br /> <br /> Then you Changed. <br /> <br /> You got lucky. You fell in with the Forsaken and were able to be given a purpose to fight for. Maybe you even found a pack who you could belong with. Maybe that Pack even convinced you that you weren't a monster doomed to destroy everything around you.<br /> <br /> But you know the truth: you're Cursed. <br /> <br /> There is no happily ever after for creatures like you. Your happiness was temporary - it couldn\u2019t have lasted. You were discovered, and one by one your previous family hunted down those who took you in.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a few months since you buried all that was good about your life. You\u2019ve been running on the hunt since then - and the Siskur-Dah is so tiring, but you've finally found the trail of the one responsible for orchestrating the death of those you cared about. <br /> <br /> Your quest for vengeance is at its end.<br /> <br /> Or is it?</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\">The Pack:</span><br /> <br /> <i>Abhraham Apostol</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, a Cahalith of the Blood Talons, is a man broken by his past as an outlaw who took advantage of the turmoil prior to the War of Northern Aggression. He tried to escape that past, fell in with a pack of military-minded Blood Talons, and thought that he could finally repent. He was wrong. His pack was slaughtered, and though he lost himself to the Death Rage in the last moments of the attack - he still woke up alive \u2026 and utterly alone. </span><i>- Played by Viskarenvisla<br /> <br /> Moose</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, a Rahu of the Hunters in Darkness, is our only actual descendant of our Werewolf-Hunting Family: the Argents. He abandoned the lucrative silver-mining business and went into the virgin wilds of the western Kentucky Territory to become a fur trader. He played both sides: werewolves and hunters against each other and finally picked when he Changed under the Full Moon. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\">He fell in with a motley pack consisting of outcasts and even got married. Of course, his Family didn\u2019t approve of his new life, and one night after a Hunt, the pack was ambushed. Moose remembers losing himself to the Rage, that he woke up with his pack scalped and left for scavengers, and that his wife was nowhere to be found. Moose has the Giant Merit and plays it up constantly. </span><i>- Played by GriffinGuy<br /> <br /> Zosia</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, an Ithaeur of the Bone Shadows, is a free woman of color. She was born in Haiti, and migrated to Louisiana with her mother after some nasty trouble on the island. There, she noticed the same curse that had afflicted her childhood community had followed to their new life and she met some Hunters who knew how to help her find a way to fix it permanently. Of course, when she found herself Changed under a crescent moon, she fled everything she knew to keep that bloodthirst off her family. She found a small pack of Bone Shadows who, like her, were mostly freed people of color and they found a home in the bayous. When the Argents caught up to her, they made sure Death Wolf\u2019s children met their Firstborn in the most painful ways possible. Zosia has been running ever since. - </span><i>Played by ZeiGal<br /> <br /> Pally</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, a grumpy Great Horned Owl is one of two animal companions that Moose has inducted into the new pack. Pally doesn\u2019t really understand the plight of the ground-bound owlets, but he is happy to soar above them.</span><br /> <br /> <i>Toro</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, a young and inquisitive ferret is the second animal companion. Quick and dexterous, he\u2019s slowly learning how to bring back the shinies that Moose is training him to fetch.</span><br /> <br /> <i>Ixtil</i><span style=\"color:#141414\">, a fire-spirit that has been bound into a fetish-tattoo on Zosia's back. Since then, it's become, well, friendly with the Ithaeur.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T10:13:36-07:00","id":1333117,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Chapter One: Vengeance<br /> <br /> <i>Wisdom is but the beginning of Fear\u2026</i><br /> <br /> Three shadows move across the tumbled rocks and broken crevices that define the southern edge of the rail line. The wood and iron are new, still smelling of the dust and manpower that arranged this lattice across the land. None of them have spied rust anywhere on the metal which suggests that it had yet to see a true winter.<br /> <br /> Three shadows are panged by hunger and thirst. Exhaustion snaps at their heels and threatens them with it\u2019s cold, uncaring embrace. One slip-up, one misjudgment, and their hunt would be over - their oaths unfulfilled.<br /> <br /> The front range mountain landscape of the new Colorado territory is mostly virgin old-growth forest and high-altitude prairie. The fevered craze of the Pike\u2019s Peak Gold Rush that welcomed in the 1860s is now a useless fantasy. They\u2019ve passed many a small town abandoned to rot in their grave pits, the skeletons of civilization stripped bare of any life that once inhabited them.<br /> <br /> Three shadows follow the rail-line, tracking the coal-fed beast that sheltered the one man who had his name written on every scrap of correspondence they\u2019d uncovered, had his hands in every plot they unburied, and his stench on every trail they\u2019ve ran down.<br /> <br /> Malcolm Willams. His name was well-known to them now, his aura of menace a haunting caul that coated their restless sleep. They would not dream well, nor know the true meaning of rest until he was brought low under their claws.<br /> <br /> For one of them, this Hunt comes with a heavier burden against their soul.<br /> <br /> For Malcolm Williams is Moose\u2019s younger brother. The Rahu remembers Malcolm with a smile always on his face and eagerness burning in his heart. He had been ambitious, sure, but Moose can\u2019t remember Malcolm consumed with greed.<br /> <br /> Of course, that was over thirty years ago, and Moose has Changed in both morals and physicality. Malcolm is little more than a stranger now.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(Play began with a -1 to most physical-based rolls to showcase the wear-and-tear of constantly hunting. The Siskur-Dah might be sacred, but it is demanding. They start with a Perception roll. Apostal fails, while Moose scores an exceptional with 3. Zosia gets a respectable 2 )</span></span><br /> <br /> Apostol is currently in the Dalu, his Union cap and jacket battered by time and battle. He jogs to keep pace with Moose\u2019s loping stride.<br /> <br /> A city-born boy, Apostol is too used to the dust of the cities clogging his nose, and the noise of civilization pressing always - constantly up against his ears to really know how to open his senses to the world around him. Besides, he\u2019s currently busy running through the names of those he knows has wronged him. He\u2019s too inwardly focused. He knows that Luna wears her Eloduth mask, and will judge the end of this hunt as any Goddess would.<br /> <br /> He checked the action of his shiny, cherry-wood red repeater, a beautiful piece of work with a gilded brass mechanism that fired as many bullets in a minute as a whole squadron working in concert.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're gettin' close,&quot; Apostol growls in a tobacco-scarred voice. &quot;How you wanna take on the guards?&quot;<br /> <br /> Zosia is far more used to the wet and humid bayous, and the way scents linger in fur and on skin, but she\u2019s adapted. Currently, she smells the acrid burn of coal on the air without the associated heat - and when she tilts her head to listen along the rail-line, she doesn\u2019t feel vibrations on the track: the train has stopped somewhere up ahead.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s in the small, wiry Urhan-shape, and the endurance of that shape assists her to keep stride with Moose even in his Hishu-guise.<br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Train stopped. Not long.&gt;</i> Zosia growls to the others. It\u2019s hard to convey abstract concepts in the wolf-tongue, but she manages.<br /> <br /> Moose realizes they\u2019re still about several minutes out from catching up to their quarry if the train has stopped. He notices that they\u2019re moving into the shadow of a rock-quarry as the mountain around them is scarred by dynamite. It seems like the destination is one of a hundred mining outposts struck up in the Front Ranges after the devilish promise of gold. However, he doesn\u2019t smell horsemeat, or livestock. There\u2019s not even wood-smoke in the air, just the stale coal slowly drifting off. As he peers around, he notices the fog rolling off the heights like a waterfall, obscuring and painting the dark shrub-brush and the skree of the foothills into ink against the grey-washed night.<br /> <br /> \u201cScope them out first,\u201d Moose answers Apostol before he shifts down into his enormous Urhan-guise. No one could mistake him for anything but a wolf. As he Changes, he sends a trained signal up into the sky for Pally.<br /> <br /> Pally makes his presence known with only the softest rush of wingbeats, a noise that only Moose can actually hear - and then follows it up with a three-toned call. A blot of ink against the starlit sky, they track him more by the absence of light than anything else at the moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ya'll don't want that train goin' anywhere I reckon I got a solution for that,&quot; Apostol drawls, and reaches into his army jacket, pulling forth a stick of dynamite with a wild look in his eyes.<br /> <br /> Zosia glances up to catch the dynamite in the Apostol's hand, taking a wary sidestep from him. <i>&lt;Patience.&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(I allow Zosia and Moose to make a Wits+Survival roll here to determine what, if any advantages they\u2019ll get from their scouting endeavor. I also rolled for Pally. Naturally, no one succeeds but the bird.)</span></span><br /> <br /> The area of the front range that the three wait in is mostly shrub-brush that has fought to obtain footholds on the craggy rocks, and what little of the forest is cut back to allow the rail a wide berth on both sides.<br /> <br /> They slow down, but keep moving, and realize they\u2019re moving along a subtle incline and turning around a natural bend in the hill. It\u2019s typical for mountain-construction as companies try and avoid destabilizing the mountain and risking rockfall - and spending money on expensive explosives out here.<br /> <br /> It also blocks any sort of visual vantage they might claim, though.<br /> <br /> Pally sweeps back into view a few minutes later and lands on a jut of rock to chirrup away. Neither Zosia or Apostol can understand the bird yet. <i>&lt;&lt;The snake is resting. I see movement throughout the belly. I see two humans walking along the scales holding their long talons. There is a cave and I see two more humans carrying nests into it.&gt;&gt;</i><br /> <br /> &quot;What's your critter got?&quot; Apostol is impatient. Typical for his tribe, and it\u2019s just been his nature since he was a kid.<br /> <br /> Moose translates the owl's understanding of the situation,<i> &lt;Train's stopped. Activity inside. Two gunmen outside. Two carrying something into the cave.&gt;</i> He wasn't sure what nests would refer to. Logs? Baskets? He wasn't sure. <i>&lt;Targets in the train, outside train. Need to... hmm... Need to get closer. Need to get one of us onto train. Make sure it doesn't leave...&gt; </i><br /> <br /> &quot;Then we oughta hit hard and fast. Strike 'em before they have a chance to react and get outta here - we should get set up, I can take a pot-shot at one of the meat bags what's armed,&quot; Apostol whispers, adjusting his army-cap and checking the iron-sights of his repeater. &quot;One of us ought to take out the driver...then move in, mop 'em up before they can pull the iduth-fil if we can.&quot;<br /> <br /> Zosia starts to speak when Apostol does first and then stops to consider his addition. She frowns, as much as a wolf could, and chuffs a bit at the grass beneath her. &lt;That is up to you two. I will check the cave when you distract them.&gt;<br /> <br /> <i>&lt;You take the gunmen, I get onto the train and turn it into an abattoir, Zo takes the cave.&gt;</i> Moose growls low, codifying his plan as he sneaks into position.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;[We'll paint the town red,]&quot;</i> Apostol threatens and takes his Urhan-guise, handsome with long, silver-brushed fur. <i>&quot;[Zo you be careful, I know you ain't a soldierin' type like us. If it's too hot you lemme know, this guy can take care of hisself.]&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(Dex/Wits + Stealth as the pack moves into position. Apostol spends a WP, and everyone scores 2 success.)</span></span><br /> <br /> The pack comes across the pitiful reminder of greed-run-rampant. They maneuver into position in the remains of a small mining outpost, left to rot away in the damp and the dust. There's a scattering of buildings, five or six at most. Two larger ones, most likely the worker barracks and the office where the foreman would have sat and brooded on his earnings.<br /> <br /> There are others, one-room rotten-wood squares that give no hint as to what they were used for. This is a dead place, so why would Malcolm come here?<br /> <br /> Apostol and Moose spy two men walking the length of the train with guns braced in their hands. They're on guard, their eyes scanning ... inward towards the outpost and the mine\u2019s opening.<br /> <br /> <i>&lt;There's something else they're afraid of, better watch out for it while we do this&gt;</i> Moose says, looking at the gunmen on the train before he starts to look for a way inside. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;[Fear is the mind-killer big guy...we'll scare 'em better than any cave boogeyman,]&quot;</i> Apostol replies.<br /> <br /> Moose moves along the train. He counts off six cars, one of which is filled with coal, two of which are typical passenger cars, two closed cars without windows - and a back car that has the caboose door open and revealed shelves of what smells like salted meat and stale produce. Supplies, most likely. The closed cars would require breaking into them, but the others look easy enough to slip in without too much notice.<br /> <br /> Apostol breaks off from Moose and moves with Zosia into the abandoned outpost to find a relatively put-together wood shack that gives him a decent vantage on the opening of the mine shaft and the train, though it blocks Moose from his sight as the Rahu favors the train-side the guards aren't currently scanning.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(As the pack prepares and gets into position, I throw an Environmental Tilt at them: <i>Fog Rolls In</i> As the fog creeps in off the mountains, sight becomes a problem. -2 to Perception and Rolls Requiring Ranged Accuracy. +2 to Stealth-based rolls. )</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>WHHHHHIRRR</i><br /> <br /> The heavy side-door along the innermost closed-cart moves with a shuddering groan, eeking open and revealing a dark, cramped space within. As it opens, the scent of unwashed flesh pours out and hits Moose, first. He can smell the people within it, the stink of fecal matter and aged urine, the cloying fear, the desperation that pours like molasses into the air.<br /> <br /> Creeping along, Moose looks to the passenger cars, deciding that would be his point of entry. When the stink comes out, he decides that now is the time. Despite his lupine body, he would begin with this form, his smallest form, and from there he would grow.<br /> <br /> &quot;KEEP TOGETHER,&quot; A third gunman yells, this one hopping out from the closed car. If the stink of the dark space bothered him, it doesn't show as he lands on the graveled ground and starts to shove out a herd of people.<br /> <br /> There's no one color of destitute that sticks out as the mass is brought forward. Apostol spies cruel slave brands on some of the black folk, from his time running the Plantation heists. He recognizes a smattering of Chinese thanks to his time in the U.S Army drafting them into building the rails on the Kansas territories. There\u2019s also white folk too, bodies dirty and cheeks gaunt from lack of food.<br /> <br /> The two guards up atop the train snap into attention, their sights aimed at the milling crowd gathering below them.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;[God of the Apocalypse, bringer of Fire and Chaos, to know you is to live and to serve you is to sacrifice our enemies through annihilation. Through your Howl, which will Destroy the Universe, I cry vengeance. Help me to overcome Kuruth and deceit, to establish your law of death and justice. Grant this through the blood I spill for you...]&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Apostol is still incredibly close to his human origins, and much of his view on his new life is filtered through his Protestant faith. As penance for his misguided youth with the Argents, Apostol also has a hard-line on slavery of any sort.<br /> <br /> He lines up a shot, aiming at the head of the closest guard patrolling the top of the train.<br /> <br /> Zosia barely manages to scramble underneath a broken awning of wood half-lost to the ground before she\u2019s discovered by three men idling around the opening of the two-horse wide gap in the mountain, bordered by newly-reinforced wooden beams: a mine-shaft. A rotted cart-line feeds into it, but they're not using it. Instead, they're carrying sealed boxes out.<br /> <br /> As she catches her breath, she sends her sight across the Gauntlet to see how the memory of this place has affected the Hisil. She senses the heat of her fiery companion, the spirit quiet but active in the tattoo that stretches across the span of her back. The Gauntlet itself is scarred heavy and thick here, unusual for a desolate place out in the wilds. Why is the gauntlet knotted and corded here like you were in the middle of a bustling east-coast town?<br /> <br /> Then her sight is across. She doesn\u2019t see the rail line. She doesn\u2019t see the buildings, even their graves. There is only the mountain with a gaping wound in its side, the darkness like a maw into the abyss itself. There is little activity here, a lattice of shimmering rope stretched across the cave to give off the impression of teeth.<br /> <br /> She is confused, what the hell is happening out here? She\u2019ll figure it out later after they\u2019ve taken down Malcolm. She stays low, growling impatiently.<br /> <br /> Where was the diversion?<br /> <br /> Moose eases into the passenger car and takes note of the private section. He smells Malcolm here, his sweat tinged with the bitter-sweet of alcohol.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s risking losing himself to the Rage, and channels that into a Killer Instinct. This doesn\u2019t need to be strung-out. He just wants Malcolm dead. He bulks into the Urshul and is now roughly the size of a Grizzly. It\u2019s become hard to move in the tight quarters, but he wants the extra weight on his side.<br /> <br /> He waits for the signal.<br /> <br /> -CRACK-<br /> <br /> A bullet whizzes out of the darkness, and the muzzle flares as the familiar retort of a Henry roars through the night. The bullet whizzes forth from the explosion...and sails just beyond Apostol\u2019s target, as the guard turned sharp at the sudden noise.<br /> <br /> &quot;Shit...&quot; Apostol curses, and lines up another shot.<br /> <br /> The crowd bolts. Like spooked sheep, the unwashed masses slam into each other in their panic to seek shelter. Some jump back into the prison they were just fed from, others crowd to the passenger cars, to the buildings, scrambling for cover. Some dive under the train itself.<br /> <br /> The guards react, guns snapping up and eyes scanning for where the shot came from. You're lucky in that the rocks reverberate the noise and hide the direct impact, but you can't rely on that too long.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(Even with 11 dice and 9-again, Apostol rolls an impressive\u2026 0. Still, our Cahalith activates Pack Triumphs Together and brings Moose up to his Initiative.)</span></span><br /> <br /> With the gunfire, Moose takes that as his chance to tear down the door. His claws rake through nearly all of the door,, leaving only splinters to shoulder through - nothing that would slow down his approach. Inside, he sees two people, Malcom who stares at the beast at his door with wide-eyes that shimmer between fear and hatred; and another man, this one black and sitting like he was crunched into his position for far too long. There\u2019s no fear in that second man\u2019s gaze. Just surprise. And hate.<br /> <br /> Mostly hate.<br /> <br /> As much as the enormous wolf can grin, Moose does, as he rushes forward, jaws outstretched to swallow Malcolm whole, snapping down like a steel trap upon his brother's flesh.<br /> <br /> There isn't much room for Malcom to go. He struggles to get his revolver out from the hostler even as he moves to try and escape Moose\u2019s jaws. In that tiny room, there\u2019s no escaping Moose\u2019s jaws.<br /> <br /> In the end, it happens without fanfare.<br /> <br /> Yes, there are screams. Yes, Moose is aware of the stumbling, blind panic of the herd as they race into the car behind him. Yes, he notices something crawling underneath the skin of the dark-skinned man as he pulls his own gun out to take his own shot at Moose\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> Moose hears the explosion of the barrel near his cheeks and barely jerks his head away just in time to avoid having it blown off seconds after achieving vengeance.<br /> <br /> But does that matter? Malcolm is crushed beneath Moose\u2019s jaws, his throat destroyed, his blood trickling down into Moose\u2019s gullet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(Moose scores 9L on his attack on Malcolm and thus the brother-killer is brought down. And even with a -3 to Moose\u2019s defense due to size and space, the second man\u2019s revolver-fire gets a zilch.)</span></span><br /> <br /> Apostol grins ferally as he takes aim a second time. This time, he strikes a gut-shot on one of the train-guards. His satisfaction is short-lived. He needs to move, as they\u2019ve pinpointed where he\u2019s shooting from.<br /> <br /> As he moves back into cover, wooden shrapnel scratches at his cheeks as a hole is blown through the rotted wood where he just braced against. A second shot sounds off, and this one slams through the wooden barrier and punches hard into his shoulder - tearing muscle. He\u2019ll have a hard time bracing the rifle against it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(Apostol scores a 6L on his shot, but payback is a bitch. Even with half-cover and the defense of the Dalu, he takes 5L in return! Apostol activates Berserker\u2019s Might to bring that down to 3L)</span></span><br /> <br /> Moose realizes that there\u2019s something twitching underneath the dark-skinned man\u2019s flesh, but he doesn\u2019t quite bring himself to care. He\u2019ll worry about it after the man is dead. He spits out his brother\u2019s spasming corpse and turns that deadly maw onto the second man. He expects it to end roughly the same.<br /> <br /> Moose\u2019s jaws clamp down around the dark-skinned guests' shoulders and he rips and tears, pulling back and expecting to take muscle, sinew, and bone with him. Instead, he feels his teeth crunch around what feels like living rock.<br /> <br /> The dark-skinned man grins. &quot;I appreciate you loosening the vessel for me, though I did like this one.&quot; He shudders, and from that wound, Moose watches as one, two, three elongated, sectioned arms covered with fine hairs and a chitinous armor pull out. At the edge of the upper arms, the hands are tipped with long, razor talons best suited for tearing and weaving thick webs... or slicing through the heavy fur of an Uratha. Those blades swing down through the closed space awkwardly but still cut deep, sliding through Moose\u2019s muscle. They stop only when they bounce against bone.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(3L on Moose)</span></span><br /> <br /> Ouch. OUCH.<br /> <br /> Apostol hisses in pain as the round breaks through his shoulder - there's a flare of silver light as a portion of his Renown comes to life, deflecting the round's velocity somewhat and preventing more catastrophic damage. It's nothing he can't handle, but it hurts like hell. The Dalu-shape is fast as he crouches in an army bull-rush after vaulting out the window, breathing heavy and fast, eyes flashing like a pair of torches in the dark as he cranks the handle of his Henry and dashes through another doorway, throwing his back up against a wall and then peeking out.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;[Fenrir...Hear me roar.]&quot;</i> He squeezes the trigger, watching as another lance of hot lead goes streaking through the flesh of the Argent closing on them. He grins, fangs ivory and sharp in the dark.<br /> <br /> Apostol aims, fires, and then rushes towards another section of broken wood as his shot punches into the gut of the nearest guard at ground level. He hears a grunt that morphs into a chittering cry that pierces through the night. Risking a glance back, he discovers the man peeling at the bullet wound, green-black ichor dripping around his fingers as he widens it, forcing himself through.<br /> <br /> Then he ducks, wood shattering around his head once again as he crouches behind cover, Another bullet slams into him, ripping open a hot graze on your side, red and raw against your ribs.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\">(3L on Apostol)</span></span><br /> <br /> <i>SKREEEEEE </i>goes the alarm. <i>URATHA</i>!<br /> <br /> He manages to catch a glimpse of the three guards from the mouth of the mine as they disappear into the fog that's now thick and heavy over the battlefield, and his sensitive ears pick out the unloading of cartridges, the plink of bullets hitting the ground. They're reloading.<br /> <br /> Shit.<br /> <br /> \u201c<i>&lt;AZLU!&gt;</i>\u201d Moose roars, too late as he recognizes the oddity of the Gauntlet, how it\u2019s too heavy. He goes for another bite, gambling on his size and power to quickly end the encounter before the Azlu can break fully out of its shell.<br /> <br /> He realizes, perhaps, that he relies too much on simple size in solving a lot of the logistics of a fight. But, he rationalizes, it's hard to mess up just crunching someone's head in one go.<br /> <br /> He manages to rip away one of the arms, the monstrous spider squealing in pain as his teeth snap cleanly through one of its limbs. A spray of green-black ichor comes out and Moose dodges before he realizes he\u2019s doing it. That ichor sizzles against the wall - eating away at the wood.<br /> <br /> &quot;NYRAAAGH, I will eat .... <i>&lt;and tear ... and make your bones into a trophy fitting a king&gt;</i>&quot; The dark-skinned man once had a pleasantly gravel-voice, low-octave and filled with presence, but it is lost to the scratching-squealing-clicking of the Azlu as it fades from English to the First Tongue.<br /> <br /> The man is gone now, replaced by a horrible spider that has no real-world match. The thing is easily as big as a grizzly, easily as big as Moose himself and growing as it sheds the last of the humanity that hid it. Six pairs of eyes stare hatefully at the Rahu as seven pairs of legs come to shake themselves free of their flesh-cage.<br /> <br /> Moose notices two more pairings of those dangerous blades, and as the spider rears up to strike, he sees the shimmer of ichor on one of them. SLICE they go, one after the other.<br /> <br /> He manages to dodge one pair of blades, but the second cuts shallow... but that's all the Azlu needs. His skin burns and his mind wavers as the pain lances up his spine.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(3A on Moose).</span></span><br /> <br /> &quot;THEY'RE BREAKIN' OUT THE <i>IDUTH-FIL!</i>&quot; Apostol roars, guessing at the meaning of a reload before the guards had even taken a single-shot. If they\u2019re bringing out silver, then the pack needs to fall back. Regroup. Reorganize. This went South - quickly.<br /> <br /> He threw his head back and let out a harsh, powerful roar, his distinctive, scarred voice ringing out into the night, a call in the tongue of wolves to fall back.<br /> <br /> Apostol manages to score a nasty shot - his bullet blowing a hole in the head of one of the three as the man fumbles to press the cartridges into the barrel. The man\u2019s form falls to the side, fingers twitching still around the bullet he holds.<br /> <br /> Behind him, the Azlu is free now and is now a spider the size of a pony. The thing is fat and bloated and skitters through the wooden debris like it was made for such a feat. It's fast, too, tearing up the ground and slicing at him with limbs that reach too damned far.<br /> <br /> Then come the shots. One after the other after the other. They're unleashing the full might on him. Where the fuck is Zosia? Where the fuck is Moose?<br /> <br /> Apostol hits the ground hard as several of those too-long limbs reach out and slice at his legs. There goes a tendon. There goes a ligament. His body struggles to heal against the damage but Azlu know how to hunt his kind too well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(Apostol gets another 5L on him! He activates Berserker\u2019s Might to throw off the Stunned Tilt and manages to save himself from wrapping into Aggravated. But he\u2019s also burning through essence.)</span></span><br /> <br /> The only saving grace is that the bullets whizz through the air above his head, allowing him to avoid the risk of silver striking into his heart.<br /> <br /> The crowd flees now, most of those who wanted to run already gone, while others still cower in place and wait for the monsters to leave. Screams and sobs fill the air. Fresh urine strikes Apostol\u2019s nose as quickly as ichor and the scent of blood does.<br /> <br /> Moose yowls in pain, the blades sinking into him. Still, while Malcolm's death was his original goal, this was his duty. This was the prey he'd been tasked with fighting. And the wolf must hunt.<br /> <br /> Deciding to use both of their unique sizes against his foe, Moose sends forth his snapping jaws as he pushes the spider against the wall, with the intent of crushing it against the train care walls, or else breaking it out of the train entirely. Moose slams the massive creature against the wall, and windows shatter. Ichor eats away at the wood, at the glass, corrodes the metal. It burns and makes his eyes water, but he avoids the brunt of it as he shoves the spider half-out the train, glass slicing through its swollen belly.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(Moose scores an impressive 5 successes on the massive Azlu, and stuns it with his Urshul ability, allowing him a chance to breathe without being hit by another swipe of those agg-blades)</span></span><br /> <br /> Moose catches the churning movement within that belly as the creature slumps over, struggling to make sense of the sudden concussive force against it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Augh-SHIT!&quot; Apostol shouts as he\u2019s thrown to the ground hard enough to smash his head. The <i>ulal </i>in his body burns fast enough to clear the fog in his thick Dalu skull as he vents blood, realizing just how badly fucked up this nightmare, mega-spider had hurt him.<br /> <br /> Spiders. Blasted, goddamn spiders. Apostol hates them, hates the way they creep under his blanket when he was sleeping. Hates the way they slice his tendons and loom as massive as a damn horse.<br /> <br /> His fingers dig into the ground as he takes a breath, reaching down, deep into his heart to that place Blood Talons go, reaching out through the inferno to touch Fenrir's gore-slicked talon. &quot;ZOSIA, A LITTLE HELP HERE DAMMIT!&quot; he shouted as his words devolved into a loud, guttural rage, scarred Gauru-howl overpowering his shout as he spun to his taloned feet.<br /> <br /> The Cahalith darts forward and grasps onto the Azlu's front claws as all his wounds close up instantaneously - the beauty of the deadly Killing Shape, its mutable grace shaped by perfect evolution. He wrestled the beast up against the wall after throwing his rifle down, kicking outward with a taloned claw at its face and raking down to rip away chitinous flesh.<br /> <br /> The rage beats at Apostol\u2019s mind and demands that he fight. A part of him sworn to the demands of a shackled god burns with shame that he would even have thought to fall back. He is a son of the Chained-Wolf, his bond forged through blood and hate and how dare he announce the retreat.<br /> <br /> Still, he can deal with the whims of the Gods later, once he\u2019s finished ripping this creature's innards out over the way.<br /> <br /> Someone screams. The crowd, frenzied now that the Killing Form is loose, surges away from between the two spiders, unable to flee. There\u2019s the smell of burned flesh but that doesn't matter. Not when he can scent this thing's death so close.<br /> <br /> And ... two spiders? What the hell had Moose found in that train?!<br /> <br /> Meanwhile \u2026 <br /> <br /> With the gunshot, Zosia takes her chance to creep past the idling guards. Between the fog sweeping over the ground, and then the sudden distraction of the firefight near the train, she manages to secure herself a perfect lead into the mine shaft itself.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">(Zosia scores an impressive 7 successes on 7 dice on her Wits+Stealth roll. This becomes important later on in the combat)</span></span><br /> <br /> There are more workers in here, some of them just as unwashed and weak as the ones poured from the train. These ones bolt like sheep as well, only to be fired upon by four men. These carry rifles, but the long-barreled guns are slung over their shoulders. Why waste expensive ammo on nobodies when you have a revolver?<br /> <br /> Five humans drop, three of them near-death.<br /> <br /> Zosia doesn\u2019t break her stealth, mourning the waste of life from the shadows. She doesn\u2019t scent Malcolm here, so she takes her time during the distraction to investigate what the guards are hauling out of the mine.<br /> <br /> The gauntlet is so thick here, she feels like she can't breathe, but she knows it's just a spiritual trick. She scouts around some of the crates; some are filled with glass bottles, green ichor within them. Others ... she thinks she hears the sound of rustling movement, as fine as blades of grass.<br /> <br /> Zosia decides as she hears the alarm calls of \u201cSilver\u201d and \u201cAzlu\u201d that it\u2019s time to head back. The word Azlu flattens her ears and spies the three men crouched behind crates, reloading to shoot her pack.<br /> <br /> So far she hasn't been noticed. Zosia creeps quickly toward the two gunmen that she couldn't stop before but now has a chance. She presses her paw firmly on the ground between them, pads warm against the cool earth that suddenly leaps up to her whim. The earth rushes up with her paws as she rears back. It surges upward, building on itself, until it\u2019s engulfing the men's mouths and noses, wrapping around to lock in place.<br /> <br /> She comes through the fog like a ghost and brings a silent, swift promise of death to the two. With the awareness that they\u2019re facing Azlu, she ensures that the earth swallows the gunmen whole to prevent the escape of any poisonous shards.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(That previous stealth roll? This is what Zosia spends her Condition on, scoring a free-shot at using Shaping to effectively sculpt an earthen prison around the remaining two gunmen. They get to suffocate, and Zosia sweeps away the threat of silver bullets in one go!)</span></span><br /> <br /> Ixtil thrums heat against her back and chases away the thoughts that might plague her from the knowledge that she\u2019s sentenced two men to death. &lt;There are more in the cave&gt; Ixtil whispers. &lt;Be wary&gt;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">(Ixtil is the fire-spirit within Zosia\u2019s fetish-tattoo.)</span></span><br /> <br /> Luna sits on her celestial throne and with a half-lidded gaze, she stares down from the circle of stars above the mountains as three of her children throw themselves into battle against ancient enemies.<br /> <br /> A debt has been paid in blood, and impassive Lunes sit vigil as a brother's lifeblood seeps into velvet seats.<br /> <br /> A threat has been exposed, and impartial Lunes mark the spill of ichor that stings the eyes and burns the Flesh-Side.<br /> <br /> As clouds drift lazily along the sky, the massive spider that was a man groggily stirs from the terrible blow struck to it, and gives the Urshul a hateful, burning look.<br /> <br /> <i>&lt;You... Cannot... Stop...Us ... All.&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T10:18:04-07:00","id":1333120,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Vengeance 1.2: </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Perhaps...&gt;</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Moose replies, in growling First Tongue </span></span></span><i>&lt;But I can stop you&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And with that, the massive wolf manages to grow even larger, not quite rearing on his hind legs, but his forelimbs rearrange into giant arms. With talons the size of saber-swords, he drives his hands into the Azlu\u2019s head. As his claws bury into several of those eyes and blind them forever, he realizes the movement at the base of the creature's abdomen too late - then the movement at your hands.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Over a hundred small crawlers burst through, ignoring the ichor, and seeking their escape; each of them the size of a small mouse, and each of them quickly being lost in the fog.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The grizzly-sized spider, caught between the windows and the Gauru struggles. Ichor drips down over Moose's talons, down his arms. It burns. It stings and eats at your skin but the intoxicating healing of the Gauru form washes it away.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Down below, the Talon and the Spider wrestle with titanic fury. Apostol growls and hisses, snapping his jaws near its hideous face as he cast it about, trying to get an advantage on the creature before it barely, just barely slipped free from his grasp - he gives a roar of outrage, stumbling forward onto all fours before recovering with lightning speed.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The slightly-smaller but no less terrifying creature Apostol wrestled with allows the Cahalith to rip through two of it's smaller pair of legs as it works to escape into the dark around the train. It's wounded, badly, and sputters as it makes halfway before collapsing. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Apostol rolls and scores 5 successes on a grapple check. The Azlu rolls and ... also scores 5 successes on a grapple check. I allow Apostol to get damage on the creature, but it manages to break away still.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The muffled screams don't register with Zosia as they should, she views the frantic clawing for any way to clear the dirt pouring into their airways as merely an afterthought. She's already moving past them into the fog, following the sounds of the battle she's already missed much of. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia slips through the mist like a shadow. Then out of the gloom, a massive spider comes at her from the southeast, limbs flailing as it begins to crawl into the rotted wooden barracks. She notices a faint rippling across its entire body.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">From the entrance to the mine shaft, a sudden cloud of black smoke hits the air, foul-smelling and bilious.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose growls out a curse at the dispersing spiders dissolving into the night. Yes, this was technically a win, as it would take years for that shard of the Spinner-Hag to regain strength such as this, but to know that they would be able to regrow stung his pride.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">With his massive quarry downed, Moose bursts out of the train car, finally feeling free to stretch his enormous bulk, which he celebrates by leaping on top of the spider that just escaped from Apostol. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&lt;</span></span></span><i>Dynamite</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">!&gt; He yells out the command as he buries his claws deep underneath the weak-points of the monstrous spider.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The long-limbed, powerful Cahalith-Gauru returned to the tall, only somewhat underweight form of Apostol, adjusting his Union cap and gazing with a mixture of skepticism and horror at Moose, as if he hadn't heard him correctly. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;You outta yer mind?! There's folk in there with what may be more o' them monsters, I ain't just sealin' 'em inside!&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He\u2019s a little ticked off that Moose has secured the final killing blow, and with the previous shame from his totem licking at his neck, Apostol\u2019s temper is running a little hotter than it should be.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He squares off against the giant Gauru, glowering.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose is struggling to keep the Gauru-form. It\u2019s hard to not give into the urge to murder ones\u2019 way through all problems. And Apostol isn\u2019t helping his control, either. As the Blood Talon shouts at him, Moose barely manages to keep from losing it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Griff rolls a 1 on a Resolve+Composure check to not descend into Death Rage thanks to not currently trying to kill something.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Dynamite. Now.&gt; </i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He snatches at Apostol\u2019s coat with a massive paw.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;The hell you playin' at anyway? You worried about witnesses or somethin'?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Herd must not know,&gt; </i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">the Rahu says, </span></span></span><i>&lt;Azlu must die. Dynamite.&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol narrows his eyes in disgust at the thought, putting a hand over where his dynamite stick was stored in his coat protectively. &quot;I'm not what the Argents say we are. You wanna hunt some Spiders, I'm game - let the Lunacy do its job and our claws do theirs.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The word witness seems to ring hollow, what with the gasping sobs and frightened breathing that comes from the spaces in the train that had been commandeered by those too injured or scared to flee into the forest.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Bodies are strewn over the rocks by the train itself. Some, half-eaten by ichor that still sizzles in the cool night breeze. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Smoke licks from the mine entrance. And above the mountain, the half-lidded eye of Luna herself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And negotiations were over, as Moose swipes again, hooking Apostol\u2019s coat with his claws. As he begins to haul in the Cahalith, Apostol rips free and snarls a warning to back off.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(I had Moose and Apostol roll Grapple-Checks. Apostol scores a whopping 5 successes again! And then, just like with the Spider, Moose rolls and \u2026 ALSO scores 5 successes, leaving it in a tie!)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Jesus H. Christ-&quot; the Blood Talon swears as he stumbles backwards and uses the reach of his rifle like a baseball bat, swinging it hard at the Gauru's head to knock him away and ward him back - it's...terrifyingly difficult to avoid the goddamn Rahu but the Cahalith is unbelievably slippery, giving as good as he gets as the two of them struggle and wrestle. He never points the barrel of the gun at Moose, using the stock or shoving with it like a staff. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(It was Apostol\u2019s earlier activation of Primal Strength that allowed him to keep toe-to-toe with a Gauru. Still, it ultimately failed.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Let go of me you hairy hermit bastard!\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When the Blood Talon managed to wriggle free from his grasp, Moose felt the fragile control over his soft rage just about snap, upon which, he reverted, his front half collapsing to the ground and taking the greater-wolf shape of Urshul.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Lunacy has limits,&gt;</i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Moose says, </span></span></span><i>&lt;You are proof of this. And these Azlu have advanced their thickening of the Gauntlet to a terrible degree. Use the damn dynamite.&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u201c You know what, you half-wit? Fine!&quot; Apostol pulls the dynamite out of his coat. &quot;You wanna be a monster, be ma guest.&quot; He turns on his heel and stalks away from Moose with a snarling curse, making toward the train car.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia barely scrambles out of the way in time, her rushing claws echoing in the thick fog before the Azlu\u2019s bulk can crush down on her. As she moves, there\u2019s a crunching of chiton and rock that announces the full arrival and victory of Moose. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">She hears the call for Dynamite, and the descent into bickering between the two males and thinks she might have something better - and would quiet them down when all is said and done.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>&lt;Burn it, Ixtil!&gt; </i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">She inhales, then breathes out air that seemingly catches and then ignites, spreading out over the sparse-grass ground. From her back, an red-gold glow appears to encompass her in its aura as it sweeps forward.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A miniature sun awakens along the sigil that traces the length of Zosia's back, and as Itxil stirs into true awakening, embers eat away at the very tips of Zosia's fur - giving the Ithaeur a crown of flame as the spirit sweeps forward and ignites those embers into a spark.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">A spark that Zosia twists into a flame that quickly chews through what little scrub is available. Hungry, and unaffected by the natural order, the flame seems to crawl along the rocky skree towards the struggling spider and the massive Gauru that hunches over it like a bear claiming a kill. The flames devour the rotted wood. Instead of rising up and chewing along the foundation and posts, the flame spreads wide, creeping along the rocks from scrub to scrub and engulfing the abandoned outpost in a wave of heat. The flame keeps coiled tight, like a net being drifted across the surface of a lake.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose shifts to Dalu as Apostol stalks away. Unfortunate that his companion couldn't see reason here, but at least he was willing to listen. He picks up the stick, walks over to Zosia and the flames the Ithaeur is doing her best to maintain control over.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Where do you think it'll seal 'em in best?&quot; He shows her the dynamite.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The little Ithaeur-wolf glances to those who have been her packmates for a mere few months, fighting. Again. The small wolf sneezes at their antics, annoyed as if they were flies on a hot, sticky day, then flicks her ears up at Moose. The warm burn of essence ripples through her as she meets Moose in Dalu as well, her eyes still a faint golden hue in dark brown. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;A few feet into the cave. Bottles and liquids been there for a while. People in it been there for too long.&quot; Her words are quick, peppered in a French-Creole accent and she gestures with her chin forward. &quot;Be best ta put them out of their misery.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose nods, walking over to the spot indicated, placing the explosive where she indicated, then walks an appreciable distance, &quot;If'n you would do the honors, firecracker?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol's sensitive ears picked up Zo's words and he felt a familiar hot strike of rage run through him like lightning. The Blood Talon had been with this group for a few months now...the outfit didn't have a name but it didn't need one. It was a temporary thing anyway - once Alice and Huel were gone, once the Creed was extinguished he was out of there and on his own, of this the bandit made no secret. He just couldn't agree with Moose or Zo on things like this...killing innocent people.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(The Creed is how Apostol knows the Argent Hunters. Alice and Huel are the former slaves Apostol ran with, and the two who ultimately betrayed him. He\u2019s got a long-term aspiration to see them dead.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Maybe back when he was just a man he'd have fought harder, maybe tossed the dynamite into the burning buildings but...somehow the loss of human life, offensive as it was, had become a little numb to him. It wasn't the War it was the Change, really.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He got onto the train, shouldering his weapon and carefully stepping through. &quot;Well...might as well make it a profitable venture,&quot; he grumbles.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Looting is a Wits+Investigation roll without form bonuses. Apostol scores a 1.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Honestly, there isn't much on the train itself in terms of interesting loot. There are Henry Rifles that Apostol believes he could pass along to the other two - or sell off when they hit civilization again. He finds ammunition, and there are some money clips tucked into the personal section - though they're soaked in the blood of a man with a crushed-throat. Malcolm, Apostol presumes - the family resemblance to Moose is there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He also finds letters, tucked into a satchel that has some fine-scented cigars. These letters, as he skimmed through them, mention the delivery of livestock to a small, front-range town just south of the mining boom-town of Denver.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Hmmm now lesse here...Ahh Jesse you'd've liked that rat-bastard of a Rahu,&quot; Apostol grumbles, thinking about one of his old packmates. Popping a satchel open, he slides a cigar into his mouth with an appraising sound, sparking it up with a match and taking a long puff as he reads through the letters, frowning.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">He tucks them away, mulling over the location and planning to look at a map. Maybe...just maybe...they'd find more Argents out there. Every Creeder they slew was not only a step closer to Alice and Huel, his ultimate prey, it also was clearly a favor for the Gauntlet. This place was oppressive for the senses, he'd just as soon get out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose heeds Zo's words and is carefully investigating the mouth of the mine shaft. It doesn't take him too much to discover broken bottles and overturned crates, the tops of them broken open, and the sides burned with three-feather wings, the Argent brand.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">They both hear movement deeper into the cave and smell smoke - though as you study and sniff, you discover that the smoke is isolated to iron carts filled with the bottles, and with papers. There's a small section that looked like it had served as a holding area but it was burned away now.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">They both knew Azlu well enough. When threatened, the spiders would pull back into the strange webs and cocoons they wove into the Gauntlet itself. As they passed by, they saw bodies on the ground. Malnourished and filthy, each body had a hole ripped through its' skull from gunfire, and - as they leaned down to get a closer look (and smell) - there were small traces of ichor around the wounds.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">They'd sacrificed their flesh vessels to escape. This operation has retreated - allowing the Azarath-hybrids to die for the nest to survive.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(What little leads were down here are now little more than ashes. The price one pays for open battle - but this loss is tempered by the awareness that they managed to take out two hybrids)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The glow from Zosia's back intensifies for a second, the fire shifting at her will and lights the explosive. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;I doubt we'll be able to get the rest of smaller spiders,\u201d</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Consarnit,&quot; Moose grumbles, kicking one of the bodies, he lets out a growl and takes the dynamite after Zosia lights the fuse. He throws it far into the mine itself. &quot;Well, least Tenderfoot over there'll be happy there's no innocents down there. Unfortunately, they've left their lil hidey-holes in them fellers' skulls.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thanks to the spirit\u2019s influence, the fuse doesn\u2019t burn down until they\u2019re both clear.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia apologizes to Ixtil about constraining it from burning everything. She feels the warmth of the spirit's presence chasing away the fog. The spirit seems happy and sated. After all, it\u2019s been allowed it to burn the last lingering memories of a place, and, if the packs noses are correct, it's also burned some of the bodies around the train.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Humans, after all, left evidence behind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">CRA-BOOM </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The mountain rumbles as the dynamite goes off. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The echo is swallowed by the formation of the geology around the pack, but the ground still shudders beneath their feet, and the humans scream in their hiding places - fearful eyes averting and heads being shoved down to avoid Apostol as he goes by.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The mine shaft collapses, rocks tumbling down over one another. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Gauntlet still feels thick and oppressive, but at least whatever horrors had been within the cave system have been sealed away for the moment.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol emerges from the train with his pack a little heavier, laden with rifles carried along his shoulder, his own carried in his right hand, readied just in case more Azlu sprang up from the dirt...although he got the sense this particular fight was over. A couple of glances thrown with fiery eyes at the humans keeping themselves hidden.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Wellp. Guess that bit o' dirty work is done, unless you're gonna take it out on these poor fools too,&quot; the Blood Talon growled spitefully as the pair as they emerged, motioning with his chin at the poor, pathetic mortals who hadn't signed up for this.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Pally swings by overhead, alighting on a train compartment. </span></span></span><i>&lt;&lt;Humans - three and ten more - run through the woods. Two of them bleed. They scatter like mice - can't track them all.&gt;&gt;</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Moose wishes he could feel relieved. He just completed his hunt, got the revenge he'd wanted for months. And he'd stymied the spiders as a cherry on it. But there was so much more. He looks to Apostol as he strolls up, and shakes his head.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;I'll leave that part of the oath on your head for now,&quot; Moose says. &quot;Good news and bad news, though. Good news is there's no innocents trapped in that mine. Bad news is it's on account that they had cobwebs for brains and their spiders vamoosed.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Blood Talon narrows his eyes, taking a long draw of his cigar, puffing it and letting the ash scatter as he shifted under the weight of the rifles he was carrying. &quot;That's no good. No good at all.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;The hell does this mean? The Argents and the Azlu are shackin' up, or were these idiots just co-opted into that nest?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Could be either. Mal was sittin' next to that massive fella without issue. Didn't give 'em a chance to explain...&quot; He looks to Zo, &quot;But maybe a dead man can tell us some tales?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol shows Moose the letters he found, and the rest of his looting rewards. \u201cFound some correspondences...ammo, guns we can sell or you can use if you feel like learnin'. Sounds like something about a livestock-move out to some mining town west of Denver...might be we can find more Creeders out there.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">As Moose suggests it, Zosia\u2019s already looking into the fog for those shapes and figures only Death could sniff out. Her search brings her back to the train. Back to the small circle of burned bodies. Underneath the train, she catches the pale silver of a girl - probably no more than sixteen, hunched down with her hands covering over her head and her face pressed against the track.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The back of her neck is bent in an awkward shape, the musculature ripped open like a slab of meat at the butcher's stall.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Unless </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">THIS </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">is the livestock,&quot; Moose gestures to the huddled masses. He silently wonders if the spiders were making nests in them. It's a sobering thought, Moose, but it makes sense with the evidence presented.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Though, what would be important enough for Malcom to sell off humans like sheep to the slaughter? Because that's what awaited them. Months of agony as the crawler devoured through their brain until it was fat enough - large enough that whatever was left of the person disappeared for the Azlu to emerge.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">And two </span></span></span><i>Azarath </i><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">- two hybrids in the same nest? What was worth that trouble to them?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol considered that possibility as well. &quot;If they were bringin' them here to get spiders in their heads, might be these ones got off lucky...but why? What's your brother doing involved in all this?&quot; Apostol tsked and put his cigar out, sliding it into the case with the others. &quot;There ain't nothin' here for us regardless. We can talk while we move, which I suggest we do.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;There's something more here,&quot; Moose says, angry and unsure, &quot;Something these critters wanted. Maybe something the Creeders wanted too.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;The longer we shit-dally around here the more people are gonna get turned into those things,&quot; he retorted just as angrily - not that this was much of a change from his typical state. &quot;'sides, I remember somebody gettin' awful handsy 'bout blowing up that cave entrance. Christ almighty...&quot; Apostol swears again. &quot;Listen, sounds like Malcolm was involved in some flesh-movin' operation that might be a lot bigger than this one line and...&quot; he noticed Zo. Talking to nothing. He motioned to her lightly.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;She's probably gonna pull some answers from nowhere. Unless you can get back inside that hole, the only other place to turn is...well...&quot; he motioned to the humans still living, cowering.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">----</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia\u2019s tired of the bickering of her two packmates, so she crosses to the train and crouches down to peer at the small silver girl. Since her old pack died, she\u2019s found it easier to deal with the dead than the living. She shifts into the Hishu, trying to be as unintimidating as possible.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Little one. Did you hear what was going on here before we came? What happened to you?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The ghost-girl doesn't lift her head at first. Just keeps herself pressed down into the dirt like she can dissolve into it. &quot;It hurt,&quot; her voice is a raspy echo. There's no tone to it, but Zosia hears it all the same. Like a chill running down her spine. &quot;It was dark. Then the monsters came. I tried to run but I fell. Then ...&quot; She spasms and contorts like she's being squished - like she's being forced down. Zosia watches the back of her neck, the muscles in her shoulders break open all over again. &quot;It got dark again.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia doesn't wince with the replaying of the girl's neck-snapping but her eyes do narrow for a second. &quot;Did they bring you by train like these people? The spider monsters you were running from?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The ghost-girl finally looks up at Zosia. Her face is destroyed on one side by what looks to have been acid. The other, well, she looks like she'd come from the bayou, like Zosia had. &quot;We was heading out for a job. I've got a little boy and he needs to eat and Momma can't --&quot; her body spasms again. &quot;Monsters. Large teeth. Claws. ...Crushing -- I can't -- I can't breathe!&quot; She wheezes, the sound scraping along Zosia\u2019s ears like nails on a chalkboard. She tries to wriggle, but she doesn't seem to go anywhere. Her back crunches inward in the perfect shape of a taloned foot.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Damn it.&quot; Zosia curses to herself, &quot;Did the monsters come by train, mama? Were they the ones who brought you here?&quot; The idea of finding the anchor to this soul crosses her mind but there isn't enough time. You cannot save everyone, her mama once told her. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The ghost shrugs, \u201cOnly monsters on the train promised food. The real ones - they came with the gunshot. They sayin they have good work out here. Help get the silver and the gold out onto the train - water the thirsty, feed the hungry. I could send back five dollars a week they promised.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">----</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Thought it could kill 'em,&quot; Moose whispers, looking exhausted. He could use some whiskey right now. If there was any left on the train. If he didn't think he'd need to be sober for what could come next.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol gives the Menina a sideways glance before turning and looking to the unfortunate mortals cowering in a place where monsters laired. He blanches just a little then takes his Hishu shape smoothly as he approaches.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Come on out ya'll. Danger's past, we're not gonna hurt ya.&quot; There was...a decided change in his voice. It wasn't any gentler, but it had a commanding, powerful quality to it - not something he used in the Army but edged by the power of the Gibbous Moon. Hard to ignore, even through the din of fear.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Apostol uses Voice of Glory to improve his Impression from Hostile to Average. That doesn\u2019t quite help, but it allows him to speak without the herd wanting to attack. He had an impressive dice-pool and a 9again to boot and scored ... 1)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol speaks with the silver-coated honey of the moonsong that birthed him, and finds himself faced with a crowd of about seven who had taken up residence back in the prison cart, one of them wielding a heavy length of iron chain. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Don't you come any closer!&quot; the leader is a grizzled, gaunt man with leathery, tanned skin and a snaggle scar that drew up his left side of the mouth, positioning himself between Apostol and the others. &quot;You ain't taking us nowhere.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol put up his hands and stopped where he was. &quot;Easy there with that chain feller, none of us have any intent on you. See? I ain't gonna hurt ya or take ya anywhere.&quot; He made a show of putting the guns down slowly - he didn't need them against this lot, of course. Not that he had any desire to hurt them in the first place - poor folk had gone through hell, Lunacy no less. Apostol was a bandit, not a knight. He pulled his water canteen from his belt, swished the liquid around. &quot;You folks thirsty? Hungry? We got some food and water, there's more on the train.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Everyone offering food and water.&quot; Your offer brings a sneer to the man's face. &quot;You gonna offer a bed to sleep in too? You gonna make sure the door doesn't slam as tight?&quot; Scarred-Check spits at the ground before you. &quot;We know what's out there, boy. Grizzly. Demon. Doesn't matter what you call it. We're fine. Right here. Where we've been at.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol notices that one of the persons behind him seems more receptive to the idea of actually having something to eat, but they stay tucked back away from the entrance. The entire car, underneath the stale urine, human waste, and filth reeks of fear. These people are terrified - it drips from their pores.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Ya'll're free to do just as you wish, I got no quarrel with your affairs.&quot; Apostol didn't take offense - guy was being tough. Defending his own. He'd probably be doing the same in his place. Apostol took a step back, keeping his hands where the guy could see them. &quot;We'll take what we need, leave the rest to you, leave you to your business. As a Union Officer it's my duty to inform you there's towns about twenty miles or so South of here, back that-a-way down the mountain trails.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia notices Apostol trying to save the poor, sorry souls then continues her conversation with the ghost. &quot;Did they have a symbol on 'em? Something that looked like outstretched wings with three feathers? The ones who came with gunshot?&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Scarred-Cheek stares Apostol down. Both of them knew that if Apostol really wanted, the fight would be over before it even began. It\u2019s easy to sense the exhaustion in him, how much longer he can maintain the fa\u00e7ade?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Still, Apostol gained some information. They'd been offered food and shelter. They didn't volunteer for this, and the way he describes the battle - it\u2019s possible that Lunacy has begun to twist the truth in his mind.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The ghost-girl spasms again. &quot;It's dark. I think there's something in here with me.&quot; Her ribs are unbroken again, only the wound at her neck is there.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;Did you bring anything with you? A memento? A cloth from your baby? A necklace?&quot; Zosia realizes that she\u2019s not going to get much more from this ghost, and instead of leaving it here to haunt people - it\u2019s time to help the spirit move on to whatever awaited humans in the next world.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;A'right. Well, in good faith I gotta tell you, you're best off gettin' back the direction you came. Nothin' but trouble out in these parts, folk're real crazy out here.&quot; Apostol sets down two of the guns he found in the train for the cowering crowd, then turns to address Moose:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;They're just vagrants, destitute basically. Got roped into this with offers of basics - food, a bed, you know\u2026. Useless to us.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;More glad I killed that no-good lower-n-a-snake-belly brother a mine,&quot; Moose says, handing his packmate a tin of salted meat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol takes the tin with silent gratitude, tipping his head as he peeled it open and ate with typical army speed, eyeing Zosia. &quot;...what do you reckon she's up to? Sure is weird.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">&quot;I've had some of her tribe in my pack. Talk to ghosts and spirits more than people, but that's ten kinds o' useful, tell you what.&quot; Moose says.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia tracks through the bodies that are strewn all about and quickly picks out the body with a broken neck and cracked back. Slight heat radiate as Zosia burns with essence again and the glow under her shirt returns. She holds out a hand toward the bodies and with a wave they catch fire. &quot;Rest mama. There is no need to linger.&quot; She then returns to the men and nods. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The bodies come alight and charred flesh hits their nostrils. The shimmering specter underneath the train disappears as her body becomes ash.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The three shadows stand in the middle of a desolate gravesite - no longer even a memorial to the Company that once stood here, trying to eek out fortune from the rocks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The train - well, they could let it rest. Let it rust and decay. It would be simple enough to destroy the track to slow down the discovery of the site by the curious. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The night is long in the tooth now, the moon dipping low behind the sprawl of the mountains around you. Malcom is dead, and truthfully, all of them have honored the Hunt. Their quarry is no longer a tangible threat.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">However, he has a legacy, and what little they\u2019ve gleaned from the ashes suggests that it's worrisome - and could easily continue without his oversight. But these are questions for later.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Apostol and Moose both feel the subtle tremors of exhaustion. The Killing-Wolf demands much from one\u2019s body and they\u2019re already down on little reserves. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Zosia had not taken the form of Death, but even she feels the end of the Hunt as a weight taken off her shoulders - a hole that fatigue easily fills in.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">There's only one question remaining as the three of them stand in the swirling fog: </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">What are they going to do with their lives now?</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-29T10:39:51-07:00","id":1333127,"title":"","content":"Awesome! More actual plays are always a great thing!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-01T10:11:59-07:00","id":1333543,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">New Kid(s) In Town: 2.1</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(With the prologue out of the way and our intrepid trio beginning to get a grip on their characters, we start a few weeks later, on the tail end of the travel north to the town named in Malcolm\u2019s letters)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The wind cuts low and easterly across the grasslands as the pack travels along the section of the Cherokee Trail that cuts north along the Front Range mountains. The weather\u2019s been pretty consistently dreary for a few days now, with distant clouds threatening to break rain sooner or later over the high prairie. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The pack takes their time traveling. Apostol does quite a few meet and greets, selling off the excess Henry Rifles and scoring himself a solid chunk of change that will assist them whenever they decide to settle down.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">He also gets them access to the occasional rest-stop thanks to his connections with the U.S Military out here. Between him and Moose, the pack is never short a helping hand along the way. The further north-east they go, they start to find more and more of the little clusters of humanity along the high, craggy grassland. Here, a trading post, there a military fort, and then the parceled, fence-divided acreages suggestive of ranching. Sure enough, the past three days have been littered with sightings of cattle, and picking out the lonely ranch-estates in the distance.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The pack also talks a bit about the Azlu, and the concern that they stumbled over something that wasn\u2019t just an isolated incident. The whole thing stunk of an operation that traveled a little further than any of them were happy with - and their only lead was the town they were approaching.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Welcome to Colorado City. It\u2019s a young town, just about near its fifth birthday and it\u2019s already developing an interesting reputation along with the network of trails and wagon-paths that surround it. Right now, it\u2019s barely got a hundred people who consistently live there, but the population fluxes thanks to the multitude of mines that have been struck in the area thanks to the lingering dream of the 1858 Gold Rush.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">It\u2019s also in a bit of competition with Denver. Colorado City was establishing itself as a town where the oppressive rules and regulations of the encroaching U.S idea of \u2018civilization\u2019 weren\u2019t welcomed - which brought in a certain type of entrepreneur. Actual pioneers have died out - preferring the safer, regulated passes closer to Denver.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Right now though, the pack just wants to take advantage of the liquor, beds, and food that Colorado City promises to give them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(I\u2019m playing a little fast and loose with the area, and borrowing a lot from Hunting Ground: Rockies here. So, some of the history of the city and the politics that get involved might come a little earlier than expected for anyone who\u2019s a western buff - but that\u2019s ok)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As the pack arrives on the main avenue, Moose seems to be in a chatty, reminiscing mood. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Been too long since I'd made a trip inta town. Most times if we needed somethin, someone went ta trade. We were a big ol' pack though, over twenty a us, and we had folks what made most a' the stuff we needed. Even had McFlaherty, a Scots-Irish who made his own whiskey, and better'n most sold in town,&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol isn\u2019t as chatty as Moose. He\u2019s the pack\u2019s Cahalith, and his own personal vendetta is still raw and open - now that Malcolm\u2019s dead and it didn\u2019t bring him any closure. His betrayers are still out there. &quot;Twenty in a pack? We never 'ad more than ten, bloods included.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol also tries to encourage his fellows to keep some of the guns for themselves. He\u2019s currently the only one with any skill with guns. &quot;'Afore we go much further I reckon I can sell these munitions for a good price, get us some right food and drink...unless one o' ya'll wants one.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Moose immediately declines. He much prefers his bow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(We rule Athletics for archery, though I think that might be baseline?)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia also declines. She just isn\u2019t that keen on them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol doesn\u2019t take it too hard. &quot;There was this fellow I served with...Indian, Choktaw maybe, I forget. Insisted on keeping this bow he said was passed down through the family when we were out in the field. Showed us a thing 'er too. Guns're fine if you wanna make a statement and blow someone's head off but a bow hits quiet-like...people don't know you're there.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">He tries out a joke: &quot;Ya'll Menina been stickin' with rock-spears and bows since Pangaea fell, no reason to change yet huh.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">It goes over well enough. Moose chuckles, at least.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(I have the pack roll an Empathy check as they get into town. Zosia succeeds with a 4, while the guys only score 1 each. Along with their passive perceptions, and the pack gets a little feel for the area)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The main avenue is little more than a beaten dirt road but there are two dozen wooden buildings lined up alongside it. Apostol quickly distinguishes where the law is, where the saloons are, and where\u2019s the best place to buy and sell whatever the pack needs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As Apostol is the only one who had been a city-boy when he changed, the sudden shift in noise levels doesn't throw him off too badly. The sudden barrage of scents good and bad doesn\u2019t overload him- and though he quickly picks out horseflesh (and excrement), smoke, gun oil, booze, sex, blood, urine, and the basic unwashed scent of civilization - he keeps his head.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The other two, well, they\u2019ve forgotten what it\u2019s like to be pressed in by so many noises, sights, smells, and the constant awareness of the humans around them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">For such a small town, the press of bodies is unnaturally heavy. Its awkward keeping track of each other as the three of them are jostled as they make their way. Men and women crowd the street almost equally. Boys hawk for their stores while several of the southern saloons have a girl or two outside, fanning themselves lazily in the early morning heat, their interest more on the conversation with each-other than striking up business. It's still early - the regulars wouldn't be walking by for a while to come.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">For the most part, Apostol and Moose are left alone, but Zosia - the pack can see the looks she receives. Most are open, curious stares as a freed colored woman in this part of the country isn't quite that common - especially with the war going on back east. There are a few that are cruder - eyeing her as something exotic, and some that even stare with open hostility.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Moose glares openly back at the crowd. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol doesn\u2019t, figuring that a bunch of humans doing what humans tend to do isn\u2019t worth it. Besides, if someone did start trouble, the pack could easily take them on. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Ah, Blood Talons - always gearing up to throw-down).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia is used to the looks, and she doesn\u2019t care - though she notes the more hostile stares because it\u2019s better to be aware of someone who could ambush you later. &quot;We should see if the Argent have any standin' here. We'll need to check the Hisil too. Later.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol agrees. &quot;Let's get a drink and have a siddown then eh? I could use some music. We could also do some with some salted pork, more water, maybe I can find some dynamite...&quot; that\u2019s said with a harsh look Moose\u2019s way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Moose doesn\u2019t even acknowledge it. &quot;This is a minin' town. Dynamite's in high demand,&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Moose seems to be right. Beyond the hawkers and the working girls, most of the men are dressed in rough coveralls and working gear suggestive of time spent underground or hard at digging.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">They pick out the rough layout of the town within the first hour, and Gods bless simple-minded town planning, but everything was laid out on a rough northwest-to-southeast grid, with the county seat and jailhouse at one end, and the establishments growing a little more, well, lively, by the time they hit the end of the northwestern stretch of the main road before it turned off to feed back into the main wagon pass up into the mountains.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The pack picks out a saloon that seems to have commandeered its\u2019 portion of the street. The music pours out from the place, and there\u2019s the sweet scent of food and drink on the air. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Resonance: Excitement, though none of the pack succeeded on the check.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol promises he won\u2019t start any fights. The other two give him a disagreeing look. As the pack heads in, they banter good-naturedly about bar-brawls, and if fancy was just a term used to jack up liquor prices.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As soon as they walk in, they get relief from the heat of the day. It\u2019s an open floor plan, with stairs leading up to an interior balcony that stretches over the ground floor to assist in people-watching. There\u2019s fifteen other folk in there, plus the bartender and the clever-handed man at the piano. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Everything about the place encourages them to sit for a bit, relax, have a good time.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">No one really gives them a second glance as they head inside. The pack, though, can feel that something seems to be watching them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As they come up to the bar, Apostol channels the Voice of Glory again, and begins to chat up the bartender. As he does, Moose does his own meet-and-greet with some of the local men who look like they\u2019ve just got back from mining. As he approaches, he overhears their conversation about a mine that\u2019s recently lost workers and is in danger of being shut down because no one\u2019s coming to work - even with a five dollars a week pay increase.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(How else does one seed plots besides strange rumors? This is my favorite tried and true method as the PCs can pick and choose what they follow.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol and the bartender trade idle conversation for a minute or so, and then Apostol starts flashing the coin he made trading. The bartender notices.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Struck it rich, huh? Let me guess, Cripple Creek finally produced something other than salt?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(A scam that some people used in the flurry of the gold rushes was to \u201csalt\u201d the discoveries to bring in bodies, or in layman\u2019s terms: plant gold into the streams to be found and strike up more rumors/investors)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol smiles and keeps up the disarming, good ol' Army Boy routine of his. &quot;Heard about some good opportunities out in these parts, though I reckon a lotta other folk have too from the looks of it...you get all sorts of odd people out here don'tcha.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Sure, that's what we pride ourselves on. There's fortune in the Rockies, apparently, and all those fortune hunters need food, drink, and pleasant company. If it's not gold they're lookin' for, then it's God, or Truth, or hell - anything that draws people out this way.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As Apostol chats with the bartender, Zosia notices that strange watching sensation has grown, and sends her sight across the Gauntlet. As she does, she realizes that they\u2019re sitting in the faram - the pale of a locus. Is it Claimed? Are there other Werewolves here already?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia looks across and sees a space not too dissimilar from the Unchanging-Side, though the interior of the saloon looks like a literal watering hole, with the grass, rock, and dirt carved into the image of chairs and tables. The bar that they sit at is gone, and replaced by an actual pool of liquor that continuously spills out and onto the floor. She glances down to that mirrored surface and finds that there are what looks to be a thousand shards of colored glass glimmering within it; and the Flesh-side reflected through. All the while strange fleshy-fans flutter around it like moths.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Zosia rolls a decent Occult and learns a few things: they\u2019re at a locus - a well tended one, and that it\u2019s occupied by a few spirits)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia sees a giant figure with a rictus grin that stretches from ear to ear. It's dressed in the three-piece waistcoats of an established gentleman, but it is not human. It has four arms, for one, and the face looks carved into soft gold. It seems to be intently staring at the reflection of Apostol in the mirrored pool as it itself stands within it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As the bartender mentions God, Moose takes a break from his conversation to fetch a bottle of whiskey and head back to the conversation with the miners. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(We determine here that Moose\u2019s Physical Touchstone is Alcoholism. Drinking helps him to forget, and if he imbibes too much, it helps to suppress the wolf too.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol doesn\u2019t really like the mentioning of God. He\u2019s paranoid - after all, the Argents thought themselves Holy-bound in their fight against Werewolves, so he presses the bartender: &quot;Prospectors come lookin' for God out here huh. Why, you got somebody tellin' folks he's just been waiting out here in Colorado for us this whole time? Here I thought he was back in Kansas.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia calls down the ancient tricks of the Ithaeur to whisper to her about the massive spirit that\u2019s a little too keen on Apostol right now. She doesn\u2019t trust it. As she studies the creature from the safety of the Flesh-side, she learns it\u2019s called Kuk-guzen, and it had to lend aid to any favor asked of it - but then ask a favor weighted fairly in return.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Seems friendly enough, right?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The bartender doesn\u2019t seem to open up to Apostol\u2019s wheedling. &quot;Son,&quot; he says, &quot;if you go looking hard enough, God will find you anywhere you desire.&quot; He sets out the extra bottle for Moose and doesn't seem to comment on the coin the pack is setting down. Neither, oddly enough, does any of the other patrons. No, they're busy setting bits out for their own drinks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Apostol has insane social pools, and at the same time, he keeps rolling 1s and 0s.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol knows when he\u2019s being stalled, so he tucks that away for another time. &quot;Mmm, well, must be lookin' wrong then I s'pose.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The bartender nods sympathetically. \u201cYour money is appreciated here anytime, and if you're interested in hearin' God speak, well, come back tonight. Might have a sermon prepared for you.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol then nudges the shaman next to him. &quot;...what're you gettin' here?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia returns her sight back to the flesh-side. \u201cA spirit that might be of use if paid correctly. It was enraptured by you.&quot; Zosia\u2019s eager to cross and interact with it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol, on the other hand, isn\u2019t quite as keen on the spirit-side of werewolf livin\u2019. &quot;Hmm...yeah, a possibility, but we ought be careful which denizens we go talkin' to afore we know if they're beholden to someone if we can. I didn't notice any turf markers on the way in here and neither did Moose or he'd've grunted somethin' about it.&quot; He shrugs, &quot;'sides, ain't found a way across.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia grins. \u201cAlready found it. The mirror. Besides, I know my way around spirits.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol blinks, impressed. \u201cHere\u2019s what I'm thinkin'...we pick up supplies. Dynamite, powder, provisions, maybe stop by a ferrier and pick out a nice brave mule to lighten the load. We should probly strike base outside o' town in the woods, much as I miss an actual bed, hide our stuff...come back tonight, maybe talk to that Denizen you mentioned and see what this uh, 'sermon' is all about.&quot; </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia nods. It\u2019s not a bad idea. Besides, right now Moose seems to be getting lost in conversation and his cups. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Apostol throws back another shot, then stands up and decides that it\u2019s time to work his magic on the crowd. He approaches a conversation about the money coming into a ranch just south of a place called Jimmy\u2019s Camp. He points out Moose as he comes over. \u201cThat one's late brother came here to buy his uh, 'livestock' if you recall. Might I be able to rustle up a few names since I heard some of that old Dixie money squirmed its way out West?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(I have Visk roll again. 6 dice to see what he can pick up through conversation+mingling. He rolls a fat 0. The dice hate Apostol when he\u2019s trying to not start fights.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">So, with that failure looming, we deem that Apostol is far too used to the schmoozing that was born in the east, along the plantations, where every word drips with false-flattery and double-meaning. As soon as he mentions 'Dixie', some of the music seems to falter, and he\u2019s giving a more suspicious look - and his trademarked Union Cap is now well-noticed. Some of the crowd wonders who he\u2019s spying for down here: the Yankees or the Confederates?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Conversation remains polite for Apostol, but it all clams up to basic, generics. No one seems willing to openly talk to him about anything now. Apostol finds himself back in that murky divide between North and South, where men spoke one word and meant another entirely. It brings him back to the fact that he never belonged back in that place, and now, even with the moonsong turning the prey to listen to his words - he\u2019s still not one of them, and they seem to know it as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Still, he makes note of the more successful ranchers, and who deferred to whom when they spoke. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Moose strikes out in his own information-gathering. The alcohol is just a little too irresistible, and as he meets with the miners (bringing over bottles to sweeten the first impressions) one of them seems to remember him.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Moose has Professional Training 5 for Fur Trapper. I rolled a % and it came up likely that he\u2019s well known in these parts. He also has the Giant Merit. Kinda hard to forget.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">So the miner introduces Moose to his buddies. &quot;This is that Grizzly Man Jose always talked up. Fella,&quot; he looks back at you. &quot;You was a lifesaver back in '59 when that frost hit early.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Grizzly Man, nice name, but I go by Moose, I just do what I can. Glad I made a good impression. These days, I'm usually clearin' out varmints and such. In fact, I just cleared out a mine a few days ago. What seems to be the trouble, fellers?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The scrawnier man hits the other man in his ribs with an elbow. The second man, being in the middle of a drink, sputters and glares as the first starts to speak. &quot;See! We can get the place open again, then make enough to head up to Denver, yeah? I'm Paolo, this is Jesse.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">The second man, Jesse, has a scar running along his left nasal fold which breaks the pattern of his stubble and gives Moose a wary glance. &quot;You just happened to clear out a mine, huh? What did you clear out of it?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(As soon as I mention the scar, Griff OOCly goes: \u201cThat guy is an Azlu\u201d. My players are paranoid.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Rattlesnakes,&quot; Moose lies, &quot;Whole messa them parked in the mines. Used ferrets. They're like the mongooses of the 'mericas. Mongeese? Them things what Injuns use ta kill snakes. Not our Injuns, the ones from Inja.\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(I had Moose roll for this\u2026 uh, interesting conversation. Even with the intriguing prospect of using mongeese to clear out rattlesnakes, Griff rolls a 0 on his social roll as well! The guys cannot catch a break.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Rattlesnakes.&quot; Jesse states flatly, and looks between Moose's bald-face lie and Paolo's exuberant grin. &quot;Paolo, you're an fucking idiota, man.&quot; He gets up. &quot;Rattlesnakes.&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">As he heads off, Paolo stares after him, then gives Moose a sympathetic look and an offer to drink with him and the third member, who offers up a name of Carlos. Moose does, and the conversation is steered back to the &quot;good ol' days&quot; as he\u2019s pressed for stories about his time in the mountains, and what exactly a mongeese is. It's hard, with the drink flowing, to really get the conversation back to the mines, but when you've got booze in hand and laughter around you, that sort of questioning can wait, right?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Moose gets lost in his glory days, which leaves us with Zosia.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia watches her compatriots mingle, and indulges in a little bit of people-watching. Mostly, everyone here seems to fall into one of three camps: miners, ranchers, or drifters. There's not much more that she can see at the surface, but she\u2019s got a suspicion that the waters ran pretty deep here. As the boys talked, she's approached by the local working girls. They're friendly, all smiles and earnestness. She\u2019s exotic, they tell her, and if she\u2019s interested in earning a bit of cash that didn't involve digging in the dirt, there was an opportunity here for her.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Zosia goes through a quick run of emotions. First, she\u2019s excited that she\u2019s propositioned because she prefers the fairer sex, and then she\u2019s upset because it\u2019s just a job offer. Then, she shotguns a drink and then bluntly sets down a fair bit of coin on the counter. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Unfortunately I already have work but company,&quot; She glances to her pack, &quot;I seem to be a bit short on. Care for a drink?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">When Zosia turns down the job offer, the working girls nod, understandingly. Then she offers them a job.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#2C82C9\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">(Zosia rolls her little pool of 4 dice and gets\u2026 1 success! She\u2019s the only one of the pack to succeed in their social carousing rolls.)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Well, we typically don't have ladies paying for the service...&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;But ... coin is coin, is it not?&quot;</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">&quot;Might last more than a few minutes too,&quot; the third lass slyly mutters with a wicked grin. Zosia is escorted from the saloon towards the back-section, around where the bar is. She figures she\u2019ll catch up with her Pack later. After all, Apostol's just heading out to buy supplies and Moose is ... well... Moose is deep in his own memories at the moment. She won't be missed for a bit.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}